From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Chapin <japhet@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:44:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] [PWA] Prevent cross-app LaunchParams leak and app_id
 desync

This CL addresses two security bugs in Web App launch parameter delivery
and tab app association tracking:

1. Cross-app `LaunchParams::paths_` / `dir_` leak across server redirect
   (https://crbug.com/574232164):
   - Enforce a structural invariant in
     `webapps::LaunchParams::set_app_id`: when `app_id_` is already
     populated (`!app_id_.empty()`) and is relabeled to a different
     `app_id` (such as when `SetLaunchParamsMetadata` updates an
     existing `LaunchParams` across a redirect to another app),
     automatically call `clear_paths()` (clearing both `paths_` and
     `can_write_`) and `clear_dir()`.

2. `WebAppTabHelper::app_id_` desynchronization and out-of-scope
   `LaunchQueue` delivery (https://crbug.com/574231826):
   - In `WebAppTabHelper::DidFinishNavigation`, for non-same-document
     primary main-frame navigations
     (`!navigation_handle->IsSameDocument()`), reconcile `app_id_` with
     `FindAppIdForUrl(registrar, web_contents()->GetLastCommittedURL())`
     whenever `app_id_ != committed_app_id`. This preserves pre-commit
     `app_id_` visibility for `ReadyToCommitNavigation` /
     `PrimaryPageChanged` observers and avoids redundant `SetAppId` /
     `ScheduleManifestAppliedUseCounter()` calls when the IDs already
     match, while ensuring aborted navigations cannot leave `app_id_`
     stuck on the uncommitted target app.
   - In `WebAppTabHelper::CanBeUsedForFocusExisting`, verify that
     `app_id_.has_value()` and `web_contents()->GetLastCommittedURL()`
     is within `app_id_`'s extended scope via
     `IsUrlInAppExtendedScope(GetLastCommittedURL(), *app_id_)`.
   - In `webapps::LaunchQueue::SendLaunchParams`, replace
     `DCHECK(delegate_->IsInScope(launch_params, current_url))` with a
     graceful early return when `!delegate_->IsInScope(launch_params,
     current_url)`. Launches that previously tripped this `DCHECK` in
     debug builds (or proceeded to mint file handles and invoke
     `EnqueueLaunchParams` on an out-of-scope document in release
     builds) are now dropped silently.

Fixed: 574232164, 574231826
Test: unit_tests --gtest_filter=WebAppTabHelperTest.*
Test: components_unittests --gtest_filter=LaunchQueueTest.*
